Optimal Solution - Greedy solution that minimizes interval removals by selecting intervals with the earliest finishing times.
                   Sort by end time and greedily keep intervals that don’t overlap—remove the rest.

class Solution {
    public int eraseOverlapIntervals(int[][] intervals) {
        // Total number of intervals
        int n = intervals.length;
        // If there are no intervals, no removals are needed
        if (n == 0)
            return 0;
        // Sort intervals by their end time (greedy choice)
        Arrays.sort(intervals, Comparator.comparingInt(i -> i[1]));
        // Count of non-overlapping intervals selected
        int count = 1;
        // Index of the last selected (non-overlapping) interval
        int prevInterval = 0;
        // Traverse remaining intervals
        for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) {
            // If current interval does not overlap with previous selected interval
            if (intervals[i][0] >= intervals[prevInterval][1]) {
                // Select current interval
                prevInterval = i;
                count++;
            }
        }
        // Minimum removals = total intervals - maximum non-overlapping intervals
        return n - count;
    }
}

Time Complexity :- O(N log N).
Space Complexity :- O(1).
